\section{Mathematical Preliminaries}
Let $(\mathcal{M}, g_{\mu\nu})$ denote a four-dimensional Lorentzian manifold. 
The Levi-Civita connection is defined by:
\begin{equation}
\nabla_{\lambda} g_{\mu\nu} = 0,
\end{equation}
ensuring metric compatibility.

The Riemann curvature tensor is:
\begin{equation}
R^{\rho}{}_{\sigma\mu\nu} =
\partial_{\mu}\Gamma^{\rho}_{\sigma\nu}
- \partial_{\nu}\Gamma^{\rho}_{\sigma\mu}
+ \Gamma^{\rho}_{\alpha\mu}\Gamma^{\alpha}_{\sigma\nu}
- \Gamma^{\rho}_{\alpha\nu}\Gamma^{\alpha}_{\sigma\mu}.
\end{equation}

The Ricci tensor and scalar curvature follow:
\begin{equation}
R_{\mu\nu} = R^{\rho}{}_{\mu\rho\nu}, \qquad
R = g^{\mu\nu} R_{\mu\nu}.
\end{equation}

The Einstein tensor is:
\begin{equation}
G_{\mu\nu} = R_{\mu\nu} - \frac{1}{2} R g_{\mu\nu}.
\end{equation}

These classical objects form the backbone of the UKG-SE tensor residual engine.

